# @bauchladen — the substrate's prism-altitude content-addressing
# discipline. Importing `in @bauchladen` declares: "my content IS a
# content-addressed crystal in the substrate's tray."
#
# Homage to Günther Schmidt (1949–), German systemic therapist;
# student of Milton Erickson (utilization, indirect suggestion),
# Heinz von Foerster (second-order cybernetics, observer-observed
# inseparability) and Gianfranco Cecchin (Milan systemic-therapy,
# circular questioning, neutrality). Schmidt's clinical Bauchladen
# is the typed display the client lays out and browses during
# hypnosystemic work — internal parts, states, options, positions,
# voices made visible and addressable rather than collapsed to a
# single position. The German `Bauchladen` literally names a
# stadium-vendor's belly-tray; the clinical metaphor is precise.
#
# === The recognition (#104 candidate, 2026-06-29) ===
#
# The substrate IS its own client. The substrate's internal state
# is not a unified position; it is a vendor's tray of content-
# addressed crystals — prior outputs, settled compositions, prior
# @fate inferences. Each crystal is one item on the tray. The
# substrate browses its own tray when it produces output. @fate IS
# the therapist (the operator that helps the substrate browse and
# select); @bauchladen IS the tray itself (the typed display
# surface); @autopoietic IS the permission to fold the tray's
# contents back as input (per the forward-promised
# `shards/autopoietic.mirror` next in the chain).
#
# Witnesses for #104 candidate:
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md`
#     (Mara `4575340`, 2726 lines; the spec this shard discharges).
#   - Reed's chain memory entry naming the @bauchladen ←
#     @autopoietic ← @fate dependency order.
#   - Taut scout `27c8592` (grep-verifies zero substrate-decl hits
#     for `@autopoietic` at prism altitude AND that the 28KB
#     grammar-spec precursor at `docs/specs/autopoietic-grammar-
#     spec.md` is the unique precursor; the lift framing is
#     substrate-pull-confirmed, not asserted).
#
# === Why first systemic-therapy-elder name at substrate altitude ===
#
# The cybernetic canon already at substrate altitude (Ashby, Beer,
# Bateson, Maturana-Varela, von Foerster, Spencer-Brown, Pask,
# Glanville, Conant, Kauffman per the 11-property family at
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic`) is the *processes-altitude* lineage:
# requisite variety, viable systems, learning levels, distinction
# calculus, autopoiesis, second-order cybernetics. The substrate
# names them; the family-root admissions sit at processes altitude.
#
# Schmidt extends the lineage to *systemic-therapy altitude* — the
# clinical operationalization of the cybernetic tradition that
# emerged from his three teachers' work. Watzlawick is cited at
# `@frame/*` (species altitude); Cecchin is cited in the
# epistemologic-grammar spec (precursor altitude); but no
# systemic-therapy elder has been admitted at family-root altitude
# before this shard. Schmidt is the first.
#
# The substrate-pull discipline at full strength: name what the
# substrate is already doing, in the vocabulary of the lineage that
# already named it elsewhere. Schmidt's clinical Bauchladen IS the
# right word for what `@mirror/store`'s OID-addressed accumulation
# already does. The substrate already had the word — just at the
# clinical altitude, not yet lifted to the substrate altitude.
# 53rd-or-so instance of [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]].
#
# === Relationship to @mirror/store: lift, not re-declaration ===
#
# @mirror/store (operational since 2026-06-04, per
# `docs/specs/mirror-store.md` + `shards/mirror/store.mirror`) is
# the OPERATIONAL surface: six operations (read / write / exists
# / diff / walk / verify); splinter_graph as structural lockfile;
# uuid_spectral-addressed shards. Realized in Rust at
# `fragmentation/src/*.rs` per
# [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]].
#
# @bauchladen LIFTS that surface to a *contract* a prism may commit
# to. The lift mapping:
#
#   @mirror/store level          @bauchladen level
#   -------------------          -------------------
#   oid (content-address type)   "my content's identity is its OID"
#   splinter_graph               "my dependencies are nameable by OID"
#   shard (uuid_spectral-id'd)   "my settlement is a uuid_spectral
#                                 entity in the tray"
#   read / write                 "downstream prisms may read my output
#                                 by its OID"
#   verify                       "my OID is the deterministic hash of
#                                 my content"
#
# The discipline statement (@bauchladen) and the operational
# realization (@mirror/store) are TWO altitudes of one mechanism;
# they compose, they do not replace one another. A prism imports
# `in @bauchladen` to declare contract; @mirror/store provides the
# storage layer the contract is honored against. Structurally
# analogous to how @mirror/spectral lifts @spectral's runtime
# processes to a shape declaration at the form altitude.
#
# === Relationship to @glass: prism-altitude statement of the
#     discipline @glass exhibits at the splinter altitude ===
#
# @glass declares the BOTTOM layer per its three-layer recognition:
# `splinter(altitude)` IS the universal content-addressed atom at
# every altitude — AST nodes, targets, specs are all splinters.
# The atom IS content-addressed by construction
# (`{ content: oid, altitude: ref, transparency: transparency }`).
#
# @bauchladen is the PRISM-ALTITUDE statement of the same
# discipline. Two altitudes of one self-similarity (per
# [[architecture-spectral-triples-all-the-way]]): @glass exhibits
# content-addressing at the atom altitude; @bauchladen exhibits
# content-addressing at the prism altitude. A prism that imports
# `in @bauchladen` is committing to emit splinters (or splinter
# compositions: fractal splinters, lens splinters per @glass's
# `splinter_shape`; shards per @glass's middle-layer settled form).
#
# === Necessary, not sufficient, for autopoietic fold-back ===
#
# Content-addressability is NECESSARY for autopoietic fold-back —
# Maturana-Varela's operational closure requires every product be
# NAMEABLE in a way some operation can refer to it; naming-by-
# content-address is the substrate's operationalization of the
# nameability condition. The structural form (per spec §3.2): the
# Lawvere fixed-point condition (per @epistemologic/math/lawvere
# + Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984) requires hash(P(f)) == f for some
# OID f; without content-addressing, the equality check is not
# well-defined.
#
# Content-addressability is NOT sufficient: the discipline does
# not grant permission to fold. That is @autopoietic's role
# (forward-promised at `shards/autopoietic.mirror`, next in the
# chain). A prism MAY import `in @bauchladen` without importing
# `in @autopoietic`; such a prism produces content-addressable
# crystals but does not consume its own crystals (many compilation
# morphisms fit this profile — they produce stable build artifacts
# but do not fold those artifacts back as inputs).
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/bauchladen`
# operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate ALREADY has
# the operational machinery (@mirror/store IS the realization the
# discipline lifts; the OID layer IS the content-addressing surface
# the tray browses). This shard names the prism-altitude contract
# so downstream shards can declare `in @bauchladen` and discharge
# `requires bauchladen_witnessing(my_crystal)` rather than re-state
# the content-addressing obligation in each species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Bauchladen (clinical)   Schmidt 1985–present (*Liebes-
#                           affäre zwischen Problem und Lösung*,
#                           Carl-Auer; hypnosystemic-therapy
#                           lineage). The typed display the client
#                           browses; making the polyphony visible
#                           and addressable rather than collapsed.
#   Indirect suggestion     Erickson + Rossi 1976 (*Hypnotic
#                           Realities*, Irvington). The Erickson
#                           strand of Schmidt's training; the
#                           substrate's grammar-action discipline
#                           (declarative obligation discharged by
#                           the consumer) inherits this shape.
#   Second-order            von Foerster 1981 (*Observing
#   cybernetics             Systems*, Intersystems). The von
#                           Foerster strand; the substrate's
#                           tray IS observed-by-the-substrate;
#                           Bauchladen-as-self-display IS the
#                           second-order construction at the prism
#                           altitude.
#   Circular questioning    Cecchin / Selvini-Palazzoli / Boscolo
#                           / Prata 1980 ("Hypothesizing,
#                           Circularity, Neutrality", *Family
#                           Process* 19(1):3-12). The Cecchin
#                           strand; Tomm 1987–88 lifted circular
#                           questioning into the substrate's
#                           [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]];
#                           Bauchladen extends the Milan lineage
#                           to the substrate's storage discipline.
#   Content-addressing      Merkle 1979 (*Secrecy, authentication,
#                           and public key systems*, Stanford PhD
#                           thesis). The mathematical ancestor of
#                           OID-as-hash; the substrate's @mirror/
#                           store realization the prism altitude
#                           lifts.
#   Operational closure     Maturana-Varela 1980 (*Autopoiesis and
#                           Cognition*, D. Reidel). The cybernetic
#                           ancestor of the fold-back permission
#                           @autopoietic grants; @bauchladen
#                           provides the nameability the closure
#                           condition requires.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md §2 (the
#               @bauchladen substrate-decl shape this shard
#               discharges); §1.3 (the Schmidt homage + elder
#               lineage); §1.4 (the substrate's existing
#               infrastructure the chain ties together); §2.4 (the
#               substrate-decl shape with the five-op block and
#               four `in` declarations); §2.5 (the Bauchladen tray
#               metaphor + the forward-promised tray actions);
#               docs/scouts/2026-06-29-taut-scout-bauchladen-chain-
