# NOTE (Landing 4 soft-cascade, 2026-07-14): @bauchladen composition is
# subject-general per Landing 4 (docs/specs/subject-bauchladen-
# visibility-and-eigenboard-loop.md e42181c R1 migration D3); the
# `provenance_record.producing_prism: ref` field may resolve to a
# subject_instance under Landing 4, not just a peer. Two-tick discipline
# preserves the peer-altitude reading for one release cycle. Schmidt
# homage unchanged. Every subject's torus interior IS the subject's
# bauchladen at that subject altitude.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981
source @arxiv/clinical/schmidt-1985
source @arxiv/crypto/merkle-1979

prism @bauchladen {
  focus crystal
  project crystal
  split crystal
  shift crystal
  settle crystal
}

# === The crystal carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming a content-
# addressed substrate element at the prism altitude. The crystal
# extends @glass's `splinter(altitude)` with a provenance field —
# splinters at @glass are opaque about WHO produced them; crystals
# in the Bauchladen tray carry provenance because the tray's
# purpose is browsing-with-attribution (downstream @fate
# inferences select crystals based on producing context).
#
# - `oid`           the content address; provided by @mirror/store.
#                   The crystal's identity IS this OID by
#                   construction (deterministic hash of content).
# - `altitude`      the substrate-ref naming where in the prism
#                   manifold the crystal lives; matches the
#                   @glass `splinter(altitude)` discipline.
# - `transparency`  the residual opacity the crystal carries; the
#                   @glass `transparency<p>` carrier parametric on
#                   altitude.
# - `provenance`    the producing-prism + tick + input-oids tuple;
#                   the NEW addition at @bauchladen relative to
#                   the bare @glass splinter.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on `oid` alone — two crystals
# with the same OID ARE the same crystal under content-addressing,
# regardless of provenance variation. Provenance is metadata about
# the crystal's production history, not part of its identity. This
# keeps the crystal's identity discipline aligned with @glass's
# splinter discipline; provenance is browsing context for the tray.
type crystal = {
  oid:          oid,
  altitude:     ref,
  transparency: transparency(altitude),
  provenance:   provenance_record,
}

# === The provenance carrier ===
#
# Browsing context for the tray. Per spec §2.5: provenance is what
# distinguishes the prism-altitude crystal from the bare @glass
# splinter; downstream selectors (especially @fate's tournament)
# use provenance to rank crystals by producing context.
#
# - `producing_prism`  the ref of the prism that produced the
#                      crystal (the substrate-decl path; e.g.,
#                      `@fate/algebra/connes` for a Connes-spectral
#                      crystal emitted by @fate).
# - `tick`             the monotone tick at which the crystal was
#                      added to the tray; the substrate's @time
#                      altitude carrier.
# - `input_oids`       the OIDs the producing prism consumed as
#                      inputs to emit this crystal; the structural
#                      witness of the production morphism.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple. Provenance is
# itself content-addressable (the provenance_record is part of the
# crystal's `content` bytes that hash to `oid`); but per the
# crystal identity contract above, only `oid` participates in
# crystal equality.
type provenance_record = {
  producing_prism: ref,
  tick:            ref,
  input_oids:      [oid],
}

# === The tray carrier ===
#
# The substrate's accumulating display surface. Per spec §2.5: the
# tray is the ACTIVE BROWSING SURFACE at a substrate altitude —
# crystals are added monotonically (the only operation is
# `add(crystal)`; removal is not in the vocabulary; the contents
# are immutable once added). Two structural implications:
#
# (1) The tray grows monotonically. This is the operational form
#     of recognition #51
#     ([[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]]):
#     H_mirror's dimension expands with each substrate-pull
#     recognition; the substrate's recognitions are crystals in
#     the tray; the tray's growth IS the Hilbert-space expansion
#     at the operational altitude.
#
# (2) The tray's transparency is a function of its crystals'
#     transparencies. Per-crystal opacities aggregate into the
#     tray-level opacity through the @glass `transparency<crystal>`
#     carrier.
#
# Trays are altitude-parametric — there is a tray at each substrate
# altitude where @bauchladen-importing prisms operate. The
# substrate's overall tray is the aggregation across altitudes;
# per-altitude trays are projections onto a single altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (crystals, opacity). Two
# trays with byte-equal crystal lists and tray-level opacities ARE
# the same tray under content-addressing.
type tray = {
  crystals: [crystal],
  opacity:  transparency(crystal),
}

# === crystallize — bytes → crystal ===
#
# The substrate's prism-altitude lift of @mirror/store.write. Given
# raw content bytes plus the producing prism's provenance, returns
# the crystal whose OID is the deterministic hash of the bytes
# (the storage write happens at the operational layer via
# @mirror/store.write; this action wraps the operation in the
# prism-altitude contract).
#
# Lifecycle: pre-crystallization the content is au (Fate-emitted
# splinters; uncommitted; per `shards/glass.mirror`'s au
# precedent); crystallization settles the bytes into a tray-
# admissible crystal. The transparency carrier reports any opacity
# introduced by the settlement (e.g., property-chain residuals).
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same
# shape as @glass's other action declarations and
# epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.produce.
crystallize(content: bytes, p: provenance_record) -> crystal { \ }

# === address — crystal → oid ===
#
# Exposes the crystal's content-address. Per the crystal identity
# contract: the OID IS the crystal's identity; this action is the
# read of that identity. Trivially total — every crystal has an
# OID by construction; the action never emits opacity.
address(c: crystal) -> oid { \ }

# === enumerate — scope → tray ===
#
# Enumerates the Bauchladen contents for a scoped context. The
# scope is a substrate-ref naming the altitude (or sub-altitude
# slice) at which the tray is browsed. Returns the tray's typed
# display surface; the consumer may further filter via @fate's
# tournament selector (forward-promised at
# `shards/fate/tournament.mirror`).
#
# The operational mirror of @mirror/store.walk specialised to the
# prism-altitude crystal type. walk returns an OID-graph; enumerate
# returns the typed crystals at the scope. Named `enumerate` rather
# than `tray` to keep the action distinct from the carrier type
# `tray` declared above; both name the same conceptual surface from
# the two grammatical sides (the noun is the display; the verb is
# the act of laying it out).
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
enumerate(scope: ref) -> tray { \ }

# === The content-addressed requires obligation ===
#
# Downstream shards declare bilateral agreement (per recognition
# #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) with the
# @bauchladen content-addressing discipline by writing the
# obligations below. The bilateral commitment: the @bauchladen-
# importing prism commits to producing crystals; the consumer
# commits to discharging the verification at the species boundary.

# Per spec §3.2 (the Lawvere fixed-point structural argument):
# the crystal's OID IS derivable from its content. The
# substrate's content-addressing exhibits this at construction
# time — hash(content) == oid. Inheritor shards discharge by
# realising the crystallization action such that the OID
# equality check holds deterministically across calls.
content_addressed(c: crystal) -> verdict { \ }

# Per spec §2.4 (the substrate-decl shape): a prism importing
# `in @bauchladen` declares well-formed crystallization across
# its content. Inheritor shards discharge by ensuring every
# output of the prism's actions is wrapped through `crystallize`
# (or composes through downstream actions that themselves
# discharge this obligation transitively).
inheritance_well_formed(p: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# The round-trip law: serialising a crystal and re-reading it
# yields a crystal with byte-equal OID. The structural property
# the @mirror/store.verify operation underwrites at the
# operational layer, lifted to the prism altitude as a discipline
# obligation. Inheritor shards discharge by demonstrating that
# their serialisation/deserialisation morphisms are content-
# preserving.
stable_identity_under_serialization(c: crystal) -> verdict { \ }

# The operational-mirror obligation: a crystal in the Bauchladen
# tray IS addressable via the @mirror/store.read operation at the
# OID layer. The bilateral form of @mirror/store's read/write
# duality: write produces an OID; read retrieves the content;
# bauchladen_addressable asserts the round-trip holds for any
# crystal admitted to the tray.
bauchladen_addressable(c: crystal) -> verdict { \ }

# === The bauchladen_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `bauchladen_witnessing(c)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement that
# the crystal `c` they hold IS a member of the substrate's
# Bauchladen — i.e., the crystal satisfies all four obligations
# above conjointly: content_addressed + inheritance_well_formed
# + stable_identity_under_serialization + bauchladen_addressable.
#
# The bilateral commitment: the @bauchladen-importing prism
# commits to declaring the crystal; the consumer commits to
# discharging the four obligations at the species boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires bauchladen_witnessing(my_crystal)` — same shape
# as chirality.chirality_witnessing(c),
# autopoiesis.autopoietic_closure_holds(s),
# variety.variety_preserving(species), and the metalogue
# `requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_X)` pattern at
# `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`.
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
# - `@autopoietic` (next family-root in the chain per spec §3):
#   inherits structurally — fold-back requires stable identity
#   for prior outputs to address. Every @autopoietic prism is
#   also a @bauchladen prism (transitive `in` declaration).
# - `@fate` (third family-root in the chain per spec §4): a
#   @fate inference emits crystals whose OIDs join the tray;
#   future inferences consult the tray; the tournament selector
#   browses with criteria. @fate is `in @autopoietic` which is
#   `in @bauchladen`.
# - `@mirror/store` (the operational layer): every shard the
#   store admits is content-addressed by construction; the OID
#   layer underwrites bauchladen_witnessing without needing to
#   declare the predicate in `requires` clauses (the storage
#   contract IS the discipline).
#
# No `requires bauchladen_witnessing(...)` clauses are added at
# THIS shard. The family-root declares the predicate; consumers
# add the clauses when they pull. Per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] the operational sibling and the
# deeper sub-shards (`shards/bauchladen/tray.mirror` with
# add/browse/lookup/select actions, per spec §2.5) follow when
# consumers pull.
bauchladen_witnessing(c: crystal) -> verdict { \ }

out @bauchladen
out crystal
out provenance_record
out tray
out crystallize
out address
out enumerate
out content_addressed
out inheritance_well_formed
out stable_identity_under_serialization
out bauchladen_addressable
out bauchladen_witnessing
